---
/**
 * Home hero: brand lockup + agent-routing console. Kept as a component so the MDX
 * page stays editable prose without a wall of markup.
 */
---

<section class="hero-bleed" aria-label="Introduction">
  <div class="hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="hero-kicker">agent skill linter</p>
      <p class="brand-lockup">sl<span>int</span></p>
      <h1>The linter for Agent Skills.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Skills are chosen in silence and followed without questions. slint catches the ones that
        never fire — and the ones that fire badly.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/rules/">Browse the catalogue</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#install">Install</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-stage">
      <svg class="route-svg" viewBox="0 0 320 220" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M20 40 C80 40, 90 110, 160 110 S240 40, 300 40"></path>
        <path d="M20 180 C90 180, 100 110, 160 110 S230 180, 300 180"></path>
        <path d="M160 20 V200"></path>
        <circle cx="20" cy="40" r="3.5"></circle>
        <circle cx="20" cy="180" r="3.5"></circle>
        <circle cx="160" cy="110" r="5"></circle>
        <circle cx="300" cy="40" r="3.5"></circle>
        <circle cx="300" cy="180" r="3.5"></circle>
      </svg>

      <div class="console" role="img" aria-label="Example slint terminal output">
        <div class="console-bar">
          <span>agent · skill route</span>
          <span class="live">linting</span>
        </div>
        <pre><code><span class="tok-dim">$</span> slint skills

skills/helper
  <span class="tok-err">10:1  error</span>    The instructions name scripts/cull.py,
                 which is not in the bundle
                 <span class="tok-rule">bundle/no-dangling-path</span>
                 <span class="tok-dim">↳ Add the file, or take the reference out.</span>
                 <span class="tok-dim">  https://agentskills.io/specification</span>

   <span class="tok-warn">3:1  warning</span>  The description never says when to use this
                 <span class="tok-rule">description/says-when</span>
                 <span class="tok-dim">↳ Append “Use when …” followed by the situation.</span>

<span class="tok-ok">2 problems across 1 skill.</span>
1 of them are computed fixes: run again with --fix.<span class="cursor"></span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
